# Harbinger of the Tides at sorcery speed (CR 601.2b: the {2} is an optional additional cost that is only asked while you
# propose the spell): on turn 5 Bot1 casts it for {U}{U} (a Mox Sapphire and an Island) and declines the flash cost, since
# nothing is owed at sorcery speed. Its enters trigger targets Bot2's tapped Llanowar Elves (tapped for mana on turn 4) and
# not the untapped Grizzly Bears (refused), and "you may return" is answered yes: the Elves go back to Bot2's hand. The
# {2} is no part of the mana cost, so the Harbinger's mana value is 2 whether or not it was paid (CR 202.3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island
Island
Island
Harbinger of the Tides
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Llanowar Elves
Grizzly Bears
Forest
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harbinger of the Tides.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Harbinger of the Tides.ManaValue = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Grizzly Bears; Mox Emerald; Mox Ruby
Stack.Count = 0
